Heidelberg:
    Heidelberg Castle
        Built in 1214
        Admission cost: €11
        2 km from Old Bridge
        1 km from Altstadt
    Old Bridge
        Built in 1788
        Admission cost: Free
        2 km from the Heidelberg Castle
        Connected to Altstadt
    Altstadt (Old Town)
        Built in the 1200's 
        Admission cost: Free
        1 km from the Heidelberg Castle
        Connected to Old Bridge

    Most Popular Attraction: The Heidelberg Castle with around 1 million visitors per year

Köln (Cologne):
    Köln Cathedral
        Built from 1248-1880
        Admission cost: Free (for the main Cathedral)
        Admission cost: €12 (for the entire building)
        500 m from the Hohenzollen Bridge
        Adjacent to the Old Town

    Hohenzollern Bridge
        Built from 1907-1911
        Admission cost: Free
        500 m from the Köln Cathedral
        Connects to the Northern Edge of Old Town

    Old Town Köln
        Built during Medieval times
        Admission cost: Free
        Adjacent to Cathedral
        Connects to the Hohenzollern Bridge 

    Most Popular Attraction: The Köln Cathedral with around 6 million visitors per year

Dortmund:
    Signal Iduna Park
        Built in 1974
        Admission cost: €15 for a tour
        4 km from Football Museum
    German Football Museum
        Built in 2015
        Admission cost is €19
        4 km from Stadium
    Westfalenpark
        Built in 1959
        Admission cost is €5
        2 km from Stadium

    Most Popular Attraction: The Signal Iduna Park with around 1.8 million attendees

Mainz:
    Mainz Cathedral
        Built 975–1009
        Admission cost is Free
        300 m from Gutenberg Museum
    Gutenberg Museum
        Built in 1900
        Admission cost is €5–10
        300 m from Cathedral
    Mainz Old Town
        Built during Medieval times
        Admission cost is Free
        Walking distance from both the Mainz Cathedral and the Gutenberg Museum

    Most Popular Attraction: Mainz Cathedral with several hundred thousand visitors per year. 

Würzburg: 
    Würzburg Residence
        Built from 1720–1744
        Admission cost is €10
        1.5 km from Old Main Bridge
    Marienberg Fortress
        Built in c. 1200
        Admission cost is Free for the Grounds 
        1 km from Old Main Bridge
    Old Main Bridge
	    Built from 1476–1703	
        Admission cost is Free	
        1.5 km from Residence

    Most Popular Attraction: The Würzburg Residence with around 300,000 visitors per year

Mannheim: 
    Mannheim Palace
        Built from 1720–1760
        Admission cost is €9
        2 km from Water Tower
        3 km from Luisenpark
    Luisenpark
        Opened in 1892
        Admission cost is €9.50 adults
        2 km from Water Tower
        3 km from Palace
    Mannheim Water Tower
        Built from 1886–1889
        Admission cost is Free (exterior and surrounding gardens; no interior access)
        2 km from Palace
        2 km from Luisenpark

Most Popular Attraction: Luisenpark with around 1 million visitors per year


